---
import Base from "../../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Stage 3 — Merkle tree + cross-file DAG · enprot">
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-3">Stage 3 — Merkle tree + INCLUDE</h1>
  <p class="text-enprot-muted mb-6">Per-file Merkle structure, cross-file DAG, Merkle proofs.</p>

  <section class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">Why</h2>
    <p class="mb-3">
      Stage 1's <code>payload-hash</code> is a flat hash of segment hashes in order. That's
      enough for chain anchor integrity, but it doesn't support:
    </p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1 mb-3">
      <li><strong>Cross-file proofs</strong> — prove block X is in file Y without revealing other blocks</li>
      <li><strong>Efficient incremental hashing</strong> — re-hash after one change is O(N); a tree makes it O(log N)</li>
      <li><strong>Selective disclosure</strong> — prove a subtree without exposing siblings</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      A proper Merkle tree over the WORD-region structure gives all three. The INCLUDE directive
      extends it cross-file: a top-level manifest can reference many source files by hash, and
      verification spans the whole project.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">Tree structure</h2>
    <pre class="bg-enprot-ink text-enprot-paper p-4 rounded overflow-x-auto text-sm"><code>file_root
├── plain-segment-1 (leaf)
├── WORD-Region-A (internal)
│   ├── child-segment-1 (leaf)
│   └── WORD-Region-A1 (internal)
│       └── child-segment-2 (leaf)
├── plain-segment-2 (leaf)
└── WORD-Region-B (internal)
    └── child-segment-3 (leaf)</code></pre>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm">
      Hash function: SHA3-256. Domain separation: prefix each hash input with a byte tag
      (<code>0x00</code> leaf, <code>0x01</code> internal) to prevent second-preimage attacks.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">INCLUDE — cross-file DAG</h2>
    <pre class="bg-enprot-ink text-enprot-paper p-4 rounded overflow-x-auto text-sm"><code>// &lt;( INCLUDE 575d69f5b0034279bc3ef164e94287e6366e9df76729895a302a66a8817cf306 )&gt;</code></pre>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm">
      The hash is a CAS blob ID; the blob is itself a serialized EPT file. <code>verify-chain</code>
      walks INCLUDE references recursively (with cycle detection). Search path: <code>--include-path</code>
      (repeatable); CAS is always searched first.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">Status</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
      <li><a href="https://github.com/engyon/enprot/blob/main/TODO.finalize/24-merkle-tree.md" class="text-enprot-accent hover:underline"><code>TODO.finalize/24</code></a> — per-file Merkle</li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/engyon/enprot/blob/main/TODO.finalize/25-include-directive.md" class="text-enprot-accent hover:underline"><code>TODO.finalize/25</code></a> — cross-file INCLUDE</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Base>
